      "writtenOn": "2024-05-16T18:51:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The tag values typically for normal HW, there\u0027s just the three logical buckets -- AMC, WAKE, and SLEEP. TAG_ALWAYS mainly is all three, which logically means a \"required\" request. A request that\u0027ll always be present until the client removes it.\n\nThe other most common tag is 3, which is TAG_ACTIVE_ONLY and is just AMC+WAKE, but not SLEEP. Thus, a \"suppressible\" request that goes away automatically when the HLOS goes to sleep and restores when the HLOS wakes up.\n\nTheese tags are bitmasks as you find in this file , and all bits \u003c 8 are reserved for the aggregation \"buckets\". \n \nFor local subsystem core DRVs (which aggregates local resource votes), there are more power states than pre-defined AMC+WAKE+SLEEP, so there are the more generic TAG_PWR_ST_[0-4].\nThe first three  values align to the same bucket indexes as AMC, WAKE, and SLEEP and above these there are more PWR_ST tags than normal HW. The PWR_ST_3,4 are mainly used for PCIE HW states.",
      "parentUuid": "3142f1c1_5d58ce9a",
